## App Router: AnimatePresence for Route Transitions

Needs a persistent Client Component in layout that wraps `{children}`:

```tsx
// app/[locale]/(full-layout)/AnimationShell.tsx
'use client'
import { AnimatePresence } from 'framer-motion'
import { usePathname } from 'next/navigation'

export function AnimationShell({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  const pathname = usePathname()
  return (
    <AnimatePresence initial={false} mode="wait">
      <div key={pathname}>{children}</div>
    </AnimatePresence>
  )
}

// app/[locale]/(full-layout)/layout.tsx  (server component)
import { AnimationShell } from './AnimationShell'

export default function Layout({ children }) {
  return <AnimationShell>{children}</AnimationShell>
}
```

---

## Reduced Motion

```tsx
import { MotionConfig } from 'framer-motion'

// Globally in layout — respects OS setting
<MotionConfig reducedMotion="user">
  {children}
</MotionConfig>
```

`reducedMotion="user"` — reads `prefers-reduced-motion` and reduces durations + disables
layout animations automatically.

---

## LazyMotion (bundle size)

```tsx
import { LazyMotion, domAnimation, m } from 'framer-motion'

// In a layout or shell
<LazyMotion features={domAnimation}>
  {children}
</LazyMotion>

// In components — use `m` instead of `motion`
<m.div initial={{ opacity: 0 }} animate={{ opacity: 1 }} />
```

`domAnimation` saves ~18kb vs full `motion` import.
Use when animating many components — especially in a page that loads late.

---

## Common Mistakes

| Mistake | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| Framer Motion `x`/`y` props | These are NOT hardware-accelerated. Use CSS `translate` or pass full `transform` string |
| Key by array index on exit-animated list | Use stable ID as `key` |
| `AnimatePresence` inside the conditional | It must wrap the conditional |
| No `once: true` on `whileInView` | Content re-animates on scroll back — almost always wrong |
| `initial={true}` on root `AnimatePresence` | All children animate in on first render — use `initial={false}` |
| Forgetting `'use client'` | Framer Motion components crash in server components |
